{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For, foaming</b> — a past-tense verb from the root חומר like עכור." "<b>And it drips from this</b> — And so full is the cup, and it says of the cup that it is full — also its dregs, after the manner of great and strong wine, and the uppermost wine the wicked drink, who are not fully ripened, and the dregs according to their degree."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 75, :notes {0 "The root he cites, חומר, refers to חמר מים רבים, i.e. a verb from the paradigm of 'mighty waters'; the comparison is to עכור (troubled/roiled). His grammatical classification of כי as introducing the form is preserved as written.", 1 "The passage is textually dense and possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally. The phrase שאינם גמורים (not complete/finished) may refer to the wicked not being fully punished or to the wine not being fully refined; left ambiguous as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:38.043646872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}